<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oberto Spinola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oberto Spinola was a Genoese nobleman of the thirteenth century and leader of the Ghibelline <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spinola-family">Spinola family</a> who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oberto-doria">Oberto Doria</a>, took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> in 1270 and governed as joint Captain of the People. Their dual rule excluded the Guelph families from office and coincided with Genoa's victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> at Meloria and the growth of its trade in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oberto-spinola.jpg" alt="Oberto Spinola" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Massimop · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coa_fam_ITA_spinola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
